From: R11T Arch Linux port <lmv600vm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] h264: request decode-order output

Firefox creates and submits only three VA surfaces before its first
vaSyncSurface call.  With display delay enabled, the firmware can hold the
initial IDR until reorder depth is satisfied, leaving the sync with no output
and eventually failing with VA_STATUS_ERROR_HW_BUSY.  FFmpeg hides this because
it submits a larger initial batch.

Request the same decode-order output that the HEVC path already uses.  The
control maps to HFI_OUTPUT_ORDER_DECODE, so the first decoded frame becomes
available after the initial input batch instead of waiting for display-order
reordering.
---
 src/v4l2_decoder.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/v4l2_decoder.c b/src/v4l2_decoder.c
index 56cf60a..66ddfd5 100644
--- a/src/v4l2_decoder.c
+++ b/src/v4l2_decoder.c
@@ -392,7 +392,8 @@ int venus_v4l2_decoder_open(
     if (status < 0)
         goto fail;
 
-    if (decoder->coded_format == V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC) {
+    if (decoder->coded_format == V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC ||
+        decoder->coded_format == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264) {
         struct v4l2_control delay = {
             .id = V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_DEC_DISPLAY_DELAY,
             .value = 0,

--
